SCOPE — what shipped (parity with the web source)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The web `WidgetFlowDiagram` is a PURE presentational widget primitive (a shared widget building block):
  it takes `nodes: FlowNode[]` + `arrows: FlowArrow[]` + optional `compact` / `emptyMessage` and draws an
  SVG flow graph against a fixed 100x100 viewBox — arrows (web `<line>`) behind nodes (web `<circle>` +
  `<foreignObject>` icon/value + `<text>` label). There is NO fetch / React-Query / Promise in the source,
  so it has NO loading/error/stale/offline branch (the host widget that owns the query — EnergyFlowWidget,
  EnergyFlowAnimatedWidget, LivePowerFlowWidget — renders those in its own shell). Per the sibling
  presentational-primitive precedent (WidgetChartSummary 0002, WidgetComparisonCard 0003, WidgetMapView
  0008) this surface reproduces ONLY the source's REAL branches; inventing loading/error/stale/offline
  chrome would fabricate states the source does not have (documented verbatim in WidgetFlowDiagram.Adapter.swift):
    • empty leaf    (web `nodes.length === 0` -> `<EmptyState message={emptyMessage} className="py-8" />`;
                     native "never a bare box" ContentUnavailableView + a11y hint)
    • populated graph(web `<svg aria-label="Energy flow diagram">`: arrows behind node chips)
    • compact       (a REAL branch: smaller node radius 10 vs 14, the top-3-by-magnitude arrow slice
                     `[...arrows].sort(|b|-|a|).slice(0,3)`, and the 3-letter-uppercase label compaction)
    • active        (a REAL per-arrow branch: the web `dashFlow` marching-ants — a `4 8` dash whose offset
                     travels -12 viewBox units every 0.8s, scaled to the live size; off under Reduce Motion)
    • arrow tone    (a REAL per-arrow branch: web value>0 emerald / <0 red / ==0 muted + a `color?` override)

  Native mapping (no Tailwind ports, per Apple HIG + the design-token system the sibling primitives followed):
    • icon (ReactNode)                  -> optional SF Symbol name on FlowNode (Lucide -> SF Symbols at the
                                           call site: BatteryCharging->battery.100.bolt, Zap->bolt.fill,
                                           Plug->powerplug.fill, Sun->sun.max.fill, Home->house.fill, ...).
    • AnimatedNumber value decimals={1} -> a monospaced-digit Text with `.contentTransition(.numericText())`
                                           formatted to 1 fraction digit (Reduce-Motion gates the cross-fade).
    • arrowColor Tailwind classes        -> tokens: value-sign default positive->statusSuccess /
      (text-emerald/red/[var(--text-muted)]) negative->statusDanger / zero->textMuted; the web `color?`
      and the `color?` override                  override (real callers pass text-cyan/amber/yellow/blue) ->
      (text-cyan-400 / text-amber-400 / ...)      the index-stable brand chart palette (TSChartPalette),
                                                  so distinct flows keep distinct, token-driven hues, no hex.
    • SVG viewBox 100x100 + xMidYMid meet -> FlowDiagramLayout: one uniform min(w,h)/100 scale, centered.
    • fill-white/5 stroke-white/20        -> Color.TS.surfaceGlass fill + Color.TS.border hairline stroke.
  The graphic is drawn with SwiftUI `Canvas` (arrows, incl. the animated dash via `TimelineView(.animation)`)
  + positioned SwiftUI node chips — exactly the pattern the sibling `TSRadarChart` uses (Canvas graphic +
  accessible summary rather than Dynamic-Type-scaled in-canvas text).

